<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>com.airvzxf.bose-connect-gui</id>
  <name>Bose Connect for Linux</name>
  <summary>Drive a Bose QuietComfort or SoundLink over RFCOMM</summary>
  <summary xml:lang="es">Controla unos audífonos Bose QuietComfort o SoundLink sobre RFCOMM</summary>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0-or-later</project_license>
  <developer_name>Israel Roldan</developer_name>
  <update_contact>israel.alberto.rv@gmail.com</update_contact>
  <url type="homepage">https://github.com/airvzxf/bose-connect-app-linux</url>
  <url type="bugtracker">https://github.com/airvzxf/bose-connect-app-linux/issues</url>
  <description>
    <p>
      A reverse-engineered Linux port of the Bose Connect app
      originally forked from Denton-L/based-connect. This package
      is the GTK4 + libadwaita + Relm4 front-end that wraps the
      upstream <code>bose_connect</code> RFCOMM library.
    </p>
    <p>
      Features include a hero battery card with sparkline history,
      four setting tiles (noise cancelling, voice prompts, language,
      auto-off), four one-click Profiles (Focus, Travel, Home, Quiet),
      a paired-devices panel, and a live activity log. KDE Plasma 6
      notifications are wired through libnotify; persistent state
      lives at <code>~/.config/bose-connect/state.json</code>.
    </p>
  </description>
  <categories>
